          "tool_output": "Q3 REVIEW MEETING \u2014 MEETING NOTES\n==================================\nDate:      Monday, September 8, 2026\nTime:      10:00 \u2013 11:30 am PT (Zoom)\nFacilitator: Rachel Kim\n\nATTENDEES\n---------\nRachel Kim        (VP of Sales)\nClaire Fontaine   (CFO)\nPriya Nair        (CTO)\nHannah Park       (Head of Product)\nKenji Obi         (HR Manager)\nJames Okafor      (Account Executive)\nSofia Delgado     (Account Executive)\nDaniel Torres     (Product Manager)\nOscar Mensah      (Finance Analyst)\n\nAGENDA\n------\n1. Q3 Sales Review\n2. Engineering & Product Update\n3. Finance Snapshot\n4. HR Update\n5. Action Items / Q4 Planning\n\n---\n\n1. Q3 SALES REVIEW\n-------------------\nRachel Kim opened with a summary of Q3 performance.\n\n- Total revenue closed (won deals): $1,040,000 across 14 closed-won deals.\n- 22 total deals worked in the quarter; win rate 63.6%.\n- South region led all territories at $468,000 in closed revenue.\n- Largest single deal: D019 \u2014 Sofia Delgado \u2014 $198,000 \u2014 Meridian Insights Pro\n  (signed September 5, Southern enterprise account).\n- Pipeline carry-over into Q4: D007 ($7,800), D013 ($105,000), D020 ($115,000),\n  D022 ($11,000) \u2014 total pending ~$239,300.\n\nJames Okafor noted that the North region pipeline is especially strong heading into Q4,\nwith two new prospects from the BostonTech conference (see EX001 travel expense).\n\nAction: Rachel to circulate updated forecast by EOD September 9.\n\n2. ENGINEERING & PRODUCT UPDATE\n---------------------------------\nPriya Nair reported that the DataBridge connector reached 28/30 license utilisation\n(SKU-003) and a capacity upgrade is under evaluation for Q4.\n\nHannah Park flagged that Custom Dashboard Builder (SKU-009) is at 22/25 seats; renewal\nin February 2027 should include a seat expansion.\n\nDaniel Torres confirmed the new Meridian Connector - REST (SKU-005) rollout is complete.\nEleven of twenty available licenses are now provisioned.\n\nThree open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) were reviewed. Liam Chen and\nTom Reyes are owners; target closure by September 12.\n\n3. FINANCE SNAPSHOT\n--------------------\nClaire Fontaine presented a brief Q3 finance summary.\n\n- Five unapproved expense items remain outstanding (EX005, EX010, EX012, EX020, EX023,\n  EX025). Total: ~$1,050. Oscar Mensah to chase approvals by September 10.\n- Hardware spend is tracking within budget. SKU-013 (HIPAA Compliance Pack) renews\n  October 31 at $15,000 \u2014 renewal decision needed by September 26.\n\n4. HR UPDATE\n-------------\nKenji Obi confirmed headcount is stable at 15. Two engineering hire requisitions will be\nsubmitted to the board in Q4 to support the roadmap expansion outlined by Priya.\n\nNew joiner orientation materials (see onboarding_guide.md) have been refreshed for the\nupdated tool stack.\n\n5. ACTION ITEMS\n----------------\n| Owner           | Action                                              | Due          |\n|-----------------|-----------------------------------------------------|--------------|\n| Rachel Kim      | Circulate updated Q4 sales forecast                 | Sep 9, 2026  |\n| Oscar Mensah    | Chase outstanding expense approvals (EX005 et al.)  | Sep 10, 2026 |\n| Liam Chen       | Close TKT-013, TKT-016                              | Sep 12, 2026 |\n| Tom Reyes       | Close TKT-019, TKT-020                              | Sep 12, 2026 |\n| Hannah Park     | Initiate SKU-003 capacity upgrade request           | Sep 15, 2026 |\n| Claire Fontaine | Prepare HIPAA pack renewal decision memo (SKU-013)  | Sep 26, 2026 |\n| Kenji Obi       | Submit Q4 engineering hire requisitions             | Oct 1, 2026  |\n\nNEXT MEETING: Q4 Kick-off \u2014 Monday, October 6, 2026, 10:00 am PT\n",
